  "comment": "Fundamentals of Default Routes When a router is connected to the Internet, a default route is immensely useful. With a default route, the router needs to only recognize destinations that are internal to its own administrative system. The default route will forward packets destined for any other address to the Internet service provider. This negates the necessity of running Border Gateway Protocol",
